WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.286
Deep Sync helps you explore how breathing relates to your body, sleep, and recovery.

2
00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:10.178
Your Watch measures the time between heartbeats. Your iPhone sets the breathing pace.

3
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.545
On your iPhone, open Deep Sync and tap Breathe.

4
00:00:14.765 --> 00:00:17.645
Tap Generate Session, then review the instructions.

5
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.959
Set Mindfulness Breathe on your Watch to five minutes.

6
00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:26.787
Place your phone where you can see and hear it. Support your forearm, and keep your wrist still.

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.939
First, tap Breathe in Mindfulness on your Watch.

8
00:00:31.159 --> 00:00:34.679
Immediately afterward, tap Start Breathing Cues on your iPhone.

9
00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:38.312
Now settle your hands. The Watch records; Deep Sync guides.

10
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.484
During Pre, breathe naturally. Your Watch is already sampling.

11
00:00:43.704 --> 00:00:48.141
Movement can interrupt these sensitive measurements. Keep your wrist and body still.

12
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:54.550
When Deep Sync changes to Pace, follow the iPhone's sounds, haptics, and visuals.

13
00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:59.506
Ignore the Watch's vibrations and animation. Breathe gently, and stay still.

14
00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.262
Here is a shortened example.

15
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.195
When Post begins, return to natural breathing.

16
00:01:16.415 --> 00:01:20.917
Keep still until the session ends. Your Watch is still collecting heartbeat data.

17
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.935
Finishing the breathing timer does not mean the results are ready.

18
00:01:26.155 --> 00:01:31.829
Deep Sync waits for the Watch's heartbeat data to reach Apple Health. This can take several minutes.

19
00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:36.892
When available, tap Check Health Now to check again. Repeated taps are not necessary.

20
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.401
If you don't want to wait, tap Close and Continue Later.

21
00:01:41.621 --> 00:01:46.379
Your session is saved. Deep Sync checks again while it is open and when you return.

22
00:01:46.599 --> 00:01:49.159
Pending data does not mean a zero result.

23
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.142
When the data arrives, Deep Sync calculates your session results.

24
00:01:54.362 --> 00:01:57.946
When you see Session analysis complete, tap View Latest Response.

25
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:01.793
You can also find it in Breathe, under Latest Response, then Show.

26
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.344
In Breathing Response, check Signal and coverage first.

27
00:02:06.564 --> 00:02:12.601
Then compare your heart rate variability, shown as R M S S D, across Pre, Pace, and Post.

28
00:02:12.821 --> 00:02:18.411
Pre is your starting point. Pace shows the immediate response. Post shows what remains afterward.

29
00:02:18.631 --> 00:02:23.217
Unavailable values are not zero, and one session does not prove better sleep.

30
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.424
If you track sleep, review Today the next morning.

31
00:02:27.644 --> 00:02:31.143
Use Progress to explore patterns across your sessions and nights.
